# #127, ADR-0910: a mutation in the core build runs the way spec v0.2 describes it — through its
# provider, answering one ActionResult row per target — with no change plan, protection or
# recovery around it, because the build has none; and a mutation of a target whose provider is
# compiled out meets the provider's absence rather than a missing command.
case: a mutation in the core build acts through its provider and reports its rows
profile: core
run: |
  cd /tmp
  ono -c 'let s = "written by the core build"; $s | write file core-note.txt | select operation status | to json'
  cat core-note.txt; echo
  ono -c 'remove file core-note.txt | select operation status | to json'
  test -e core-note.txt && echo "STILL THERE" || echo "removed"
  ono -c 'start service nothing-by-this-name' 2>&1 | head -1
exit: 0
stdout-contains: written by the core build
stdout-contains: "status":"success"
stdout-contains: removed
stdout-contains: Ono-Sendai-E0401 provider.unavailable
stdout-not-contains: STILL THERE
stdout-not-contains: Ono-Sendai-E0104
